I'm not an often frequenter to this corner of the internet, but I am a
fan of Nethack and I respect the game.

That being said, I had an odd occurence today while playing.  I'm no
expert, and have been playing on and off for about 8 or so years, but
this was new to me.

I was on the bottom of the mines after capturing my luckstone.
Unfortunately I had also captured a lodestone and was doing my best to
get out of a jam.  I couldnt carry much stuff up the stairs with me,
so I dropped all my junk on the floor in a sack and kept only the bare
essentials.

A couple floors up I came across a stone giant, but being fully
satiated (I stuffed up first since I couldn't carry any rations) I
decided to tin him.  I luckily had a tinning kit nearby, so I grabbed
the tin and went back downstairs to wait off my satiation.  I only had
a 9 str at the time, so I think it would have definitely helped out a
lot.

While I was at the bottom of the mines wasting time I noticed the
message "you feel an odd wave of telepathic power" or something along
those lines.  Basically the "heads up mind flayer" message.  I pop on
my blindfold to use my esp or whatever, but I dont see any
mindflayer.  What I DO see is a monster, stuck on the bottom half of
the map who is changing his appearance every 10 turns or so.

I probably spent something like 200 turns waiting for my satiation to
dissapate, and watched him change from a rogue, to a samurai, to a
dragon, to a soldier dude, bee, invisible a few times (guess he
changed into something i couldnt see with esp) and finally some sort
of uber lich.  He then warped next to me and gave me a touch of death.

So what the hell was that?  What kind of monster can change into
anything they want and have the powers of what they change into?  Is
that a camelion?  If so, since when are camelions so damn powerful to
be able to instantly own you if they by chance turn into a goddam mega
lich??

I would also like to add that there were multiple monsters in the
area, and only 1 of them was changing.  I think this rules out the
